&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Small katakana vowels&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Small katakana vowels—ァ・ィ・ゥ・ェ・ォ—are used mainly to write loanword sounds that the basic chart does not contain. They also form one モーラ with the preceding kana.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;table class=&#34;table-centered&#34;&gt;
  &lt;thead&gt;
      &lt;tr&gt;
          &lt;th&gt;Small kana&lt;/th&gt;
